    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d878">

                <pb facs="0795" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.6200/41a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ritter</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 346</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    telegrams have been received from the consular representatives of this
                    Government at numerous cities abroad reporting that there are no Swiss consuls
                    at those places to whom German interests can be turned over. For example, I am
                    advised that there are no Swiss consular officers at Barbados, Cairo,
                    Martinique, Hongkong, Azores, Lourenço Marques, and Port of Spain.</p>
                <p>I should be greatly pleased if you will ascertain by telegraph the wishes of the
                    German Government as to what disposition it desires to have made of its
                    interests at such places where there are no Swiss consular officers.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
